         ],
         "text": [
            {
               "text": "#### Introduction\n\nIn recent decades, scientists have made incredible measurements that changed the way we see the universe. The most surprising discovery is that **our universe is expanding** -- it is growing in every direction.\n\nThis means that every star, every planet, and every galaxy we observe today was not in the same position billions of years ago. Everything is moving away from everything else!\n\nBut this is not the only conclusion we can draw. If the universe is expanding now, it must have been smaller in the past. In this class, we will explore this fascinating idea and understand why we need a new mathematical operation -- **division** -- to describe how everything in the cosmos is shared.",
               "source": null,
               "date_time": null,
               "isTable": false,
               "imgdesc": "",
               "format": "markdown",
               "PostMention": ""
            }
         ],
         "desc": null,
         "next": "b2c3d4e5-f6a7-4b8c-9d0e-1f2a3b4c5d6e",
