         "text": [
            {
               "text": "#### Universe History\n\nIf the universe is expanding today, it must have been much smaller in the past. Scientists have confirmed this through many experiments over the last century.\n\nTable 1 shows some of the most important discoveries that helped us understand the history of our universe. About **13.82 billion years ago**, everything we see today was concentrated in an extremely tiny space.",
               "source": null,
               "date_time": null,
               "isTable": false,
               "imgdesc": "",
               "format": "markdown",
               "PostMention": ""
            },
            {
               "text": "|Discovery|Description|Sources|\n|---|---|---|\n|Age of the Universe (<htdate0>)|Updated to 13.82 billion years|<htcite0>|\n|Size of the Universe (<htdate1>)|Updated to 94 billion light-years|<htcite1>|\n|Size of the Universe (<htdate2>)|Updated to 30 billion light-years|<htcite2>|\n|Size of the Universe (<htdate3>)|Updated to 25 billion light-years|<htcite3>; <htcite4>|\n|CMB (<htdate4>)|Confirmation of the first radiation in the universe|<htcite5>|\n|Size of the Universe (<htdate5>)|Updated to 4 billion light-years|<htcite6>; <htcite7>|\n|Expanding Universe (<htdate6>)|Evidence that the universe is not static|<htcite8>|\n|Size of the Universe (<htdate7>)|Updated to 280 million light-years|<htcite9>|\n|Size of the Universe (<htdate8>)|Updated to 300,000 light-years|<htcite10>|",
