            {
               "type": 0,
               "uuid": "6006cb3a-9409-4d2a-999c-e4c74249f563",
               "text": "ESA",
               "page": "https://www.esa.int/ESA_Multimedia/Images/2018/07/Planck_s_view_of_the_cosmic_microwave_background2",
               "date_time": {
                  "type": "gregory",
                  "year": "2025",
                  "month": "09",
                  "day": "17"
               }
            }
         ],
         "text": [
            {
               "text": "#### The Cosmic Microwave Background (CMB)\n\nOne of the most important measurements in the history of science is the **Cosmic Microwave Background**, or simply **CMB**.\n\nThe CMB is the oldest light in the universe -- radiation created just a few hundred thousand years after the Big Bang, when the universe first became transparent. Before that, the universe was so hot and dense that light could not travel freely.\n\nIn <htdate0>, Arno Penzias and Robert Wilson accidentally discovered this radiation (<htcite0>), confirming a key prediction of the Big Bang theory. Later, the ESA Planck satellite mapped this radiation in detail, giving us a beautiful picture of the baby universe.",
                "source": [
                   {
                      "type": 1,
                      "uuid": "587cdba4-cefb-4df9-8514-2e50ccf88739",
                      "text": "Penzias, A. A., & Wilson, R. W.",
                      "page": "https://doi.org/10.1086/148307",
                      "date_time": {
                         "type": "gregory",
                         "year": "1965",
                         "month": "",
                         "day": ""
                      }
                   }
                ],
                "date_time": [
                   {
                      "type": "gregory",
                      "year": "1965",
                      "month": "-1",
                      "day": "-1"
                   }
                ],
               "isTable": false,
               "imgdesc": "",
               "format": "markdown",
               "PostMention": ""
            },
            {
               "text": "<p class=\"desc\"><img src=\"https://www.historytracers.org/images/ESA/Planck_s_view_of_the_cosmic_microwave_background.jpg\" class=\"imgcenter\"/><b>Figure 2</b>: View of the Cosmic Microwave Background (CMB) through the ESA Planck mission. ©ESA/Planck Collaboration.</p>",
               "source": null,
               "date_time": null,
               "isTable": false,
               "imgdesc": "",
               "format": "html",
