      {
         "id": "f6a7b8c9-d0e1-4f2a-3b4c-5d6e7f8091a2",
         "audio": "",
         "smile": "happy",
         "source_menu": [
            {
               "type": 1,
               "uuid": "7cc05340-732f-4c3d-b260-5437670fbc99",
               "text": "Original Text",
               "page": "https://www.historytracers.org/index.html?page=class_content&arg=7cc05340-732f-4c3d-b260-5437670fbc99",
               "date_time": {
                  "type": "gregory",
                  "year": "2026",
                  "month": "",
                  "day": ""
               }
            }
         ],
         "text": [
            {
               "text": "#### Contract Yourself!\n\nNow that we know the universe was once much smaller, let us try to feel what contraction means.\n\nPlace your finger on the circle below and watch it **shrink**. Imagine everything in the universe compressing into a tiny point -- this is what scientists believe happened at the very beginning.",
               "source": null,
               "date_time": null,
               "isTable": false,
               "imgdesc": "",
               "format": "markdown",
               "PostMention": ""
            },
            {
               "text": "<center><div class=\"htCircle\" style=\"height: 40vh; width: 40vh; background-color: white; border:1px solid black;\" name=\"fig2\"></div></center><p class=\"desc\"><b>Figure 3</b>: Circle representing the contraction of the universe. Place your finger or mouse on it to see it shrink.</p>",
               "source": null,
               "date_time": null,
               "isTable": false,
               "imgdesc": "",
               "format": "html",
               "PostMention": ""
            }
         ],
         "desc": null,
         "next": "a7b8c9d0-e1f2-4a3b-4c5d-6e7f8091a2b3",
         "prev": "",
         "jumpTo": "",
